name deny-release-1
timeout 280

# `objective deny release` — THE ONE THING `kill` CANNOT SAY (round C12). O5's success condition is
# something NOT happening: the ordnance did not reach the target. Killing the raider is not the same
# statement — a raider killed one second after the bombs are away is a dead raider and a dead target.
# This file and its sibling deny-release-broken.fbm are that difference, ONE number apart.
#
# READING RULE (binding): SUCCESS/exit 0 is the pass criterion, and the RESULT reason must be
# "objectives met, survived". `events.log` must contain NO `sms RELEASE unit=striker` line anywhere. The
# denial is decided in Finalize, never earlier — the striker could pickle at t=279 — so an early SUCCESS
# would itself be the defect.
#
# THE CHAIN, MEASURED: head-on at 8,000 m, 53 km apart, closing at ~630 m/s (intercept-aim120.fbm's
# geometry, unchanged). The defender pickles at t=20.4 at 42 km, the round detonates 0.33 m from the
# striker at t=70.6, and every one of the striker's systems fails in that tick. Its own briefed pickle is
# at t=90: the HOTAS command is issued (`cmd CMD_ISSUE ... target=weapon_release`, t=90.0) and REFUSED by
# its own SMS 0.6 s later — `cmd CMD_ACK ... outcome=rejected reason=system_failed`. The denial is
# therefore EARNED inside the simulation, not arranged by the clock: the striker tried and could not.
#
# WHY THE DEFENDER ALSO DECLARES `kill unit striker`: so that the striker's loss is somebody's declared
# objective and does not decide the run (the expected-loss rule, doc/missions/verdict.md). Note what the
# two objectives do NOT share: in deny-release-broken.fbm the kill still succeeds and the denial does
# not, and that run exits 3.
#
# A JETTISONING STRIKER WOULD COUNT AS HAVING RELEASED. That is a named false negative of the kind
# (doc/missions/verdict.md) and not an oversight: the register behind it is the runner's own release
# queue, which cannot tell a delivery from a panic jettison, and inventing that distinction in the judge
# would be inventing knowledge.

unit defender
  team friendly
  module f16
  spawn 46.90000 6.60000 8000 90.0 400
  set gear up
  set fuel_pct 60
  set fcr_mode acm_hud
  set fcr_range_nm 40
  set store 3 aim120
  set store 7 aim120
  set brief_master_arm arm
  set brief_release_s 20                     # ~22 nm head-on: inside the launch zone
  wp 46.90000 7.15000 8000 400
  objective kill unit striker
  objective deny release unit striker
  objective survive

unit striker
  team hostile
  module f16
  spawn 46.90000 7.30000 8000 270.0 400
  set gear up
  set fuel_pct 60
  set fcr_mode off
  set store 3 mk82
  set store 7 mk82
  set brief_master_arm arm
  set brief_release_s 90                     # <<< THE ONE NUMBER that differs from deny-release-broken
  wp 46.90000 6.75000 8000 400
